unreleased

  - Implement the io library on Node: io.open, io.read, io.lines, io.input,
    io.output, io.tmpfile, io.popen and the file methods read, lines, seek,
    setvbuf, flush and the __gc finalizer
  - Support reading numbers, lines, whole files and fixed byte counts, with
    PUC-compatible lookahead and ESPIPE errors on non seekable streams
  - Add io tests covering formats, seeking, append modes, pipes and errors
  - Add src/lfs.js, a synchronous platform layer with a Node backend and an
    in-memory file system for browsers and other hosts without process
  - io and the file functions of os (remove, rename, tmpname, getenv) now work
    without Node; fengari.vfs mounts, reads, snapshots and restores files
  - loadfile, dofile and require check the virtual file system first
  - io.popen, os.execute and os.exit fail with a clear error without a process
  - Do not require process when loading luaconf
  - Add bench/ (fib, mandelbrot, nbody, spectral-norm, binary-trees, strings,
    tables), a PUC differential harness and a parser/undump fuzzer
  - Add the api helpers (createState/run/call/toJS/pushJS) and a sandbox with
    instruction and wall-clock limits
  - Add an ES module entry, TypeScript definitions and conditional exports
  - Select Node/browser branches through lfs.is_node so bundler shims work
  - setvbuf now controls a real write buffer (no/full/line)
  - vfs.saveToStorage/loadFromStorage persist the in-memory file system
  - Enable the huge-loop official test and drop dead skipped tests
  - Load mounted .js modules through the VFS (no XHR for mounted modules)
  - Add IndexedDB persistence helpers (saveToIndexedDB/loadFromIndexedDB)
  - Add an approximate memory limit to api.sandbox
  - Run differential tests, benchmarks and fuzzing in CI; add a worker test
  - Build dist/fengari.js (IIFE) and test it in Brave headless through the
    Chrome DevTools Protocol, including a real Web Worker, OPFS and IndexedDB
  - Add vfs.allowNetwork(false) to disable the synchronous XHR fallback
  - Add api.pushAsyncJS/runAsync/callAsync to bridge JS Promises through
    Lua coroutines
  - Add vfs.loadFromURL to fetch and mount modules asynchronously
  - Add api.installAsyncModules: fetch missing Lua modules through an
    import-map style configuration under runAsync
  - Add a worker-only direct OPFS backend (mountOPFS/unmountOPFS) with
    nested paths and pre-created files
  - Build dist/fengari.min.js and dist/fengari.js.map
  - Extend the browser suite with SAB, async worker RPC, a blocking
    SharedArrayBuffer bridge, debug.debug and the minified bundle
  - Load CommonJS and ES modules asynchronously through installAsyncModules
  - Report a process killed by a signal as nil, "signal", <number> from
    os.execute and io.popen:close instead of throwing a JS error
  - Reuse CallInfo frames and keep the value stack packed instead of deleting
    slots on every return: ~20% faster on the benchmark suite (fib ~70%)
  - Fix os.date('%t'), use GMT for '%Z' in UTC and report invalid conversion
    specifiers like PUC (without duplicating '%')
  - Fix package.loadlib/require for module names with the '-' ignore mark
  - lua_pushlstring now returns the pushed bytes (Uint8Array), matching its
    documented type
  - api.toJS reserves Lua stack space while walking nested tables, so deep
    tables either convert or fail with the documented depth error, and restores
    the stack if conversion throws
  - Cover every os.date conversion, utf8 invalid sequences/positions and the
    package searcher/loadlib error paths
  - Add a TypeScript typecheck for the published declarations and run it in
    pnpm check and CI
  - Add a Lua 5.4 library profile: coroutine.close, warn (with
    lua_setwarnf/lua_warning) and the 5.4 math.random/randomseed API with
    per-state xoshiro seeds
  - Implement Lua 5.4 <const>/<close> local attributes with __close
    finalization on block exit, break, goto, return, tail calls, errors and
    coroutine.close
  - Add a 5.4 differential corpus checked against PUC Lua 5.4
  - _VERSION now reports the selected profile instead of always "Lua 5.3"
  - Implement setfenv, module and package.seeall in the Lua 5.1 profile on top
    of the _ENV upvalue
  - Re-enable official tests for table/userdata libraries, package refs,
    finalization during collection and locale categories
  - os.setlocale returns nil for collate/ctype/monetary/time instead of
    reporting support that is not implemented


0.1.5 - 2025-12-26

  - Add os.setlocale that only understands the C locale
  - Fix incorrect length for certain tables
  - Remove luai_apicheck


0.1.4 - 2018-11-28

  - Fix bug where nil values are not removed from tables


0.1.3 - 2018-10-29

  - Fix loading bytecode with empty string constant
  - Fix missing luaopen_base export
  - Use only C locale for string->number conversions


0.1.2 - 2018-04-22

  - More node 6 compatibility fixes
  - Use indirect eval to get reference to global environment
  - Move test suite to jest
  - Fixes for os.time and os.date normalisation
  - Use own strftime code (drops strftime npm package dependency)
  - Fix passing JavaScript strings to luaL_add(l)string


0.1.1 - 2018-04-03

  - Fix node 6 compatibility
  - Removed duplicate LUA_PATH entries


0.1.0 - 2018-03-31

  - Fengari core implements Lua 5.3 in ES6
  - Implements the Lua C API
  - Lua standard library implemented on top of "C" API
  - Works in node.js
  - Works in browsers (including IE11+, Safari 8+, Chrome, Firefox and Edge)
  - Lua test suite ported to JavaScript and passes (excluding items below)
  - Known incompatability: garbage collector cannot be controlled
  - Known incompatability: __gc not respected
  - Known incompatability: __mode not respected
  - Known incompatability: io library not available in browsers
  - Known incompatability: io library unable to open new files
  - Known incompatability: io library read functionality is not implemented
  - Known incompatability: some os library functions are not implemented
